Package: reproimage
Title: Integrity, Provenance and Reproducibility Checks for Scientific Images
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Pablo", "Sánchez-Núñez", email = "psancheznunez@outlook.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-7845-9506"))
Description: Fingerprints scientific images with file and pixel SHA-256
    checksums and with difference and perceptual hashes computed in eight
    orientations, and lists pairs that are identical or visually similar,
    including rotated, flipped and re-contrasted copies. Writes a
    self-contained HTML report and an 'RO-Crate' provenance record. Implements
    a written algorithm specification shared with the 'ReproImage' Python tool
    and is tested against the same synthetic reference images, so both give
    identical results. Results describe visual relations between images, not
    misconduct. See Sánchez-Núñez (2026) <doi:10.5281/zenodo.23881635>.
